    <h4>Firmware update</h4>
    <p>Upload a signed BBF to this Pi, transfer and verify it through the negotiated RME FILE protocol, then explicitly start the printer bootloader.</p>
    <div class="control-group">
        <label class="control-label">Upload to Pi</label>
        <div class="controls">
            <input type="file" accept=".bbf" data-bind="event: {change: chooseUpload}">
            <button type="button" class="btn" data-bind="click: uploadToPi, enable: pendingUpload() && !piUploadActive()">Upload to Pi</button>
            <div class="progress" data-bind="visible: piUploadActive">
                <div class="bar" data-bind="style: {width: piUploadWidth}"></div>
            </div>
            <p data-bind="visible: piUploadActive, text: piUploadStatus"></p>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="control-group">
        <label class="control-label">Firmware on Pi</label>
        <div class="controls">
            <div class="rme-firmware-controls">
                <select class="rme-firmware-select" data-bind="options: firmwareFiles, optionsText: firmwareLabel, optionsValue: 'name', value: selectedFirmware, optionsCaption: 'Choose firmware on Pi'"></select>
                <div class="rme-firmware-action-row">
                    <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary" data-bind="click: stageFirmware, enable: canStage">Upload candidate</button>
                    <button type="button" class="btn btn-danger" data-bind="click: stageAndFlashFirmware, enable: canStage">Upload and flash…</button>
                    <button type="button" class="btn btn-danger" data-bind="click: flashFirmware, enable: canFlash">Flash verified candidate…</button>
                </div>
                <div class="rme-firmware-action-row rme-firmware-secondary-actions">
                    <button type="button" class="btn" data-bind="click: unstageFirmware, enable: canUnstage">Unstage from printer…</button>
                    <button type="button" class="btn" data-bind="click: deleteFirmware, enable: selectedFirmware() && !firmwareBusy()">Delete Pi copy…</button>
                    <button type="button" class="btn" data-bind="click: cancelFirmware, visible: firmwareBusy">Cancel transfer</button>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="progress" data-bind="visible: firmwareActive">
                <div class="bar" data-bind="style: {width: firmwareProgress}"></div>
            </div>
            <p data-bind="text: firmwareStatus"></p>
            <div class="alert alert-error" data-bind="visible: firmwareError, text: firmwareError"></div>
            <div class="alert alert-warning" data-bind="visible: transportRecoveryRequired">
                <strong>Printer reboot required.</strong>
                Power-cycle the printer. RME command, file, and firmware traffic is locked until reboot recovery is confirmed.
                <button type="button" class="btn btn-warning" data-bind="click: confirmPrinterReboot">I rebooted the printer</button>
            </div>
            <p class="help-block">Choose the BBF in the “Firmware on Pi” list, then upload it or upload and flash. Current firmware protects and verifies the candidate as hidden <code>/usb/FWUPD.RME</code>, but it is not armed for the bootloader until the explicit FILE FLASH handoff. Unstage removes only that protected candidate; Delete from Pi removes only the source copy. Ordinary BBFs downloaded by Prusa Connect are never treated as staged updates.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
